      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 66-year-old female presented to casualty with recurrent syncopal episodes and a history of ischaemic heart disease. Initial investigations did not provide a definitive diagnosis. Subsequent CT scanning identified a giant pseudoaneurysm of the left anterior descending coronary artery, which is the largest reported to date. We include a short discussion on current literature surrounding coronary artery pseudoaneurysmal disease."},
